  "_doc": "The look of this planet's cities (visual only; planets/verdance/sites/verdance_city.gd and city_look.gd read it). Keyed by district id (districts.json). script: the city's own script (its source landmark). prop: the yard's tall prop (StreetDressing.landmark_kind). town / outskirts: the building mix on the pad and round it; any key left out keeps the value of the town kind the site would have had (VerdanceSite.KINDS, TownOutskirts.PROFILES): rings = floors [min, max] per block ring 1..3, tower = share of outer buildings that shoot up to tower_f floors, lots = share of open blocks, factory = share of works fronts, ruin = broken-off share [ring 1, beyond], houses = detached houses, mid / far = floors near and far, warehouse = share of shed blocks, streets = asphalt strips through the outskirts. walls: [texture, [r, g, b]] with texture red_brick | brick | render; tall_avoid: indices of the walls a building of tall_floors or more may not take; it takes one of tall_walls instead. roofs, awnings, tanks, signs, gables: colour lists [r, g, b] for roof surfaces, awnings and parasols, roof tanks, roof signs and flags, pitched roofs and domes. No roof colour may be white or grey (tests/test_cities.gd). roof_props: share of roofs (0..1) that carry each prop: tank, sign, shade (parasols), gable (a pitched roof over a low building), sawtooth (works skylights), billboard (a tall two-post hoarding), dome (a drum and dome), flag. street: the main street's dressing: stalls | containers | car_stacks | fences | banners, with street_gap = metres between pieces [min, max] and street_skip = share left out. tree_skip: share of kerb tree spots left empty. shop_names: painted name boards, each used once. boards: their board colours. landmark: sign = the text on the source landmark, blocks = block keys [x, z] the landmark may stand on (the first dry one wins; z is south, so [0, -2] is two blocks north of the yard), approach = true keeps the blocks between the yard and the landmark open so it closes the view on arrival. haze: the tint [r, g, b, a] of the air the source fouls (a local layer that lifts when the source is shut down), empty for none.",
